"<div><h3>Inteligencia artificial</h3><p class=\"meta\">Los agentes piensan y escriben con Claude. Pega aquí las claves: se guardan cifradas y no se vuelven a mostrar.{0}</p>\n      {1}</div>\n    <fieldset class=\"perfil\"><legend>Con qué trabajan</legend>\n      <label class=\"ia-op\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proveedor\" value=\"anthropic\"{2}><span><b>Claude (API de Anthropic)</b> · recomendado. Con un plan Max de Claude, el gasto sale de los créditos de API que incluye el plan (platform.claude.com); sin él, del saldo que compres allí.</span></label>\n      <label class=\"ia-op\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proveedor\" value=\"openrouter\"{3}><span><b>OpenRouter</b> · pago por uso con una sola clave (openrouter.ai).</span></label>\n      <label class=\"ia-op\"><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"respaldo\"{4}><span>Si se acaba el crédito de Claude, <b>seguir con OpenRouter</b> hasta que vuelva a haber crédito (necesita su clave abajo). Sin esto, el equipo se pausa y te avisa.</span></label></fieldset>\n    <fieldset class=\"perfil\"><legend>Clave de Claude</legend>{5}\n      {6}\n      {7}</fieldset>\n    <fieldset class=\"perfil\"><legend>Clave de OpenRouter (opcional: alternativa o respaldo)</legend>{8}\n      {9}\n      {10}</fieldset>\n    <p class=\"meta\">El tope de gasto del equipo (cuenta Claude y OpenRouter juntos) se cambia en «IA: … €», arriba. Ponle un límite también en la propia web de OpenRouter.</p>\n    <p class=\"conf-error\" role=\"alert\"></p>\n    <div class=\"acciones\"><button class=\"btn\" type=\"submit\">Guardar</button><button class=\"btn sec\" type=\"button\" data-acc=\"cerrar\">Cerrar</button></div>":"<div><h3>Artificial intelligence</h3><p class=\"meta\">The agents think and write with Claude. Paste the keys here: they're stored encrypted and never shown again.{0}</p>\n      {1}</div>\n    <fieldset class=\"perfil\"><legend>What they work with</legend>\n      <label class=\"ia-op\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proveedor\" value=\"anthropic\"{2}><span><b>Claude (Anthropic API)</b> · recommended. With a Claude Max plan, the spend comes out of the API credits included in the plan (platform.claude.com); without it, from the balance you buy there.</span></label>\n      <label class=\"ia-op\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"proveedor\" value=\"openrouter\"{3}><span><b>OpenRouter</b> · pay as you go with a single key (openrouter.ai).</span></label>\n      <label class=\"ia-op\"><input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"respaldo\"{4}><span>If the Claude credit runs out, <b>carry on with OpenRouter</b> until there's credit again (needs its key below). Without this, the team pauses and lets you know.</span></label></fieldset>\n    <fieldset class=\"perfil\"><legend>Claude key</legend>{5}\n      {6}\n      {7}</fieldset>\n    <fieldset class=\"perfil\"><legend>OpenRouter key (optional: alternative or backup)</legend>{8}\n      {9}\n      {10}</fieldset>\n    <p class=\"meta\">The team's spending cap (counts Claude and OpenRouter together) is changed in “AI: … €” at the top. Set a limit on the OpenRouter website itself too.</p>\n    <p class=\"conf-error\" role=\"alert\"></p>\n    <div class=\"acciones\"><button class=\"btn\" type=\"submit\">Save</button><button class=\"btn sec\" type=\"button\" data-acc=\"cerrar\">Close</button></div>",
